WikiMaps — data attribution & licensing
========================================

Historical borders (data/borders/)
-----------------------------------
Derived from Historical Basemaps by André Ourednik and contributors:
  https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps

Upstream license status (verified 2026-06):
  - The repository ships a single LICENSE file: GNU GPL-3.0.
  - Neither the README nor CONTRIBUTING states an explicit license for the
    DATA itself. Applying GPL-3.0 (a software license) to data is ambiguous.
  - ACTION REQUIRED before any public launch: obtain a written clarification
    of the data license from the author (e.g. a GitHub issue), and update this
    NOTICE and docs/DATA_SOURCES.md accordingly. Treat the data as GPL-3.0
    (attribution + share-alike + preserve this notice) until clarified.

WikiMaps transforms these snapshots into an enriched GeoJSON schema
(localized names, sources, numeric years). The transformed files in
data/borders/ are a derivative work and inherit the upstream license.

